OL,3,GNEWSATriple killer had 'delusions'
OL,4,Abefore attacks
OL,5,
OL,6,FA man suffering from delusions about
OL,7,Fkidnappings and paedophiles killed
OL,8,Fthree men hours after being released
OL,9,Ffrom custody, an inquest has heard.
OL,11,FAlexander Lewis-Ranwell was still
OL,12,Fwearing the grey tracksuit he had been
OL,13,Fissued while under arrest the previous
OL,14,Fevening when he killed Anthony Payne,
OL,15,F80, and 84-year-old twins Dick and
OL,16,FRoger Carter in Exeter on 10 February
OL,17,F2019.
OL,19,FHe had been arrested and released from
OL,20,Fcustody twice in the two days leading
OL,21,Fup to the killings, jurors at Exeter
OL,22,FCounty Hall heard.
OL,23,APub: 22-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBW-SW Eng NewsC Reg TVFWeather
